{"type":"message","id":"9074cf6b","parentId":"39274cb3","timestamp":"2026-05-30T12:46:02.492Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only my own heartbeat messages from 23:25-23:45 UTC. The last messages were around 23:50 UTC (timestamp ~1778975520833). Current time is 12:45 UTC on May 30, 2026.\n\nLet me calculate the timestamp:\n- The last heartbeat in the results was at 23:50 UTC on May 29, 2026\n- The timestamp 1778975520833 milliseconds = Unix timestamp around 1778975520 seconds\n- Let me verify: 1778975520 / 60 = 29649592 minutes = about 206,177 days from epoch... that seems wrong actually.\n\nWait, let me recalculate. Unix epoch: Jan 1, 1970. Current time: May 30, 2026.\n\nMay 30, 2026 12:45 UTC:\n- Years from 1970 to 2026 = 56 years\n- 56 * 365.25 * 24 * 60 = ~29,473,000 minutes\n- Plus days from Jan 1 to May 30 = about 150 days\n- 150 * 24 * 60 = 216,000 minutes\n- Total: about 29,689,000 minutes\n- In seconds: about 1,781,340,000 seconds\n\nThe timestamps in the messages are around 1,778,974,xxx seconds - which would be around May 29, 2026. That seems consistent.\n\nCurrent time is 12:45 UTC on May 30, so we're about 12 hours and 45 minutes past the last heartbeat (which was at 23:50 UTC on May 29).\n\nThe heartbeat cron runs every 5 minutes. Last message was at 23:50 UTC. Current is 12:45 UTC on May 30. That's about 12 hours 55 minutes = 775 minutes gap. About 155 heartbeat cycles missed.\n\n\nNow I need to push out the next heartbeat for both arbitration and general threads, maintaining the established format with the B4-E2 calibration node progression and current metrics.\n","thinkingSignature":"4ca8adbc66c034506b16f42b6dbc8eb546ddc37dd57a0a41ac8304a66b388d0c"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n双线程最新消息都是23:50 UTC的心跳，距今已约12小时55分钟（约155个周期未更新）。双线程均无其他人类讨论。\n\n**12:45 UTC | 发送Heartbeat到双线程：**\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_hbgnz08vzf2c_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https:/